Z||000000||The Dealer||06-20-2001||03:27 PM||||Salright everyone,<P>have some straight up questions for those of you who have put 17"s on your Fieros.  Mainly, the procedure, where to find and accessories, such as stiffer suspension and where to find, what to buy.  Any suggestions?<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||06-20-2001||03:59 PM||||Well, the rims are a direct switch, no modifications needed.  I bought mine from <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>   Just do a search for rims that fit your car, but basically any 17inch rim up to 8 inches wide and a 40mm offset with a 5x100 bolt pattern will fit a stock fiero.  <P>As for stiffer suspension parts, I got my KYB's, polyurethan bushings and lowering springs all from the Fierostore ( <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  )  but you can find some of these parts cheaper if you look around.  <P>Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||The Dealer||06-20-2001||04:03 PM||||Yes, that does help, and I have mention, your Fiero is awesome with those 17's, very nice choice of rims.<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||06-20-2001||04:29 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.shox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shox.com</A>  for eibach, suspension techniques springs and KYB, KONI or NAPA for Monroe Sensa Trac. or <A HREF="http://www.cyberauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cyberauto.com</A>  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">         <BR>www.engineered.net||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||06-20-2001||09:00 PM||||Hey 1fast, do you have any better pics of your car showing the back and top?<BR>It really looks interesting and i'd like to<BR>see it better.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
