Z||000006||Formula88||06-21-2001||10:12 AM||||Has anyone with an '88 and aftermarket rims gone to the trouble to get different offsets for the front?  I would think running the same offset all the way around, while it may work ok, would change the suspension dynamics and possibly hamper handling.  ||||reg||5
Z||000007||1FST2M6||06-21-2001||11:46 AM||||the handling change would only be noticable on a closed road course with a VERY experianced driver. my offsets are different due to wheel width/clearance issues. and me thinking i needed a wider tire... ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||06-21-2001||12:15 PM||||How about the look?  I know stock wheels with the same offset all the way around on an '88 look funny up front because they stick out farther.  Isn't this the same on aftermarket wheels?||||reg||1
